---
title: Spiced Aubergines and Potatoes with Coconut Rice
source: Roasting Tin
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 1 hour
---

Preheat the oven to 180°C. Halve the @aubergines{2} and @potatoes{500%g} lengthways, then cut the @aubergines{2} into 1cm half-moons and the @potatoes{500%g} into ½ cm half-moons, and transfer to a very large #roasting tin{}.

Mix together the @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @chilli powder{0.5%tsp} and @salt{1%tsp}, then scatter all over the @potatoes{500%g} and @aubergines{2}. Drizzle with the @vegetable oil{3%tbsp}, then mix everything together really well with your hands and transfer to the oven to roast for ~{45%minutes}.

Place the rinsed @basmati rice{300%g}, @coconut milk{1%400ml tin} and @water{100%ml} in a #saucepan{} with a tight-fitting lid, add a pinch of @salt{}, and stir well. Bring to the boil, stir, then replace the lid and simmer on a very low heat for ~{15%minutes}. Remove the lid, fluff the @basmati rice{300%g} through, replace the lid and leave to steam for a further ~{5%minutes}.

Taste and season the cooked @aubergines{2} and @potatoes{500%g}. Spoon over the @Greek yogurt{4-5%tbsp}, scatter over the @fresh coriander{15%g}(leaves only), and serve immediately with the @basmati rice{300%g}.
